From 08f1fe63590ee0caf3ff039141d42885e4334044 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:27:41 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: libipa: agc: Avoid light flicker

Lights on AC mains flicker at twice the mains frequency. With a rolling
shutter, an exposure time that is not a whole number of flicker periods
lets each line integrate a different amount of light, and the frame shows
horizontal bands that move from frame to frame.

Support the AeFlickerMode (Off, Manual) and AeFlickerPeriod controls in
the common AGC algorithm with the mean luminance implementation. With a
manual flicker period, ExposureModeHelper::splitExposure() shortens an
exposure time of at least one period to a whole number of periods and
raises the gain to keep the exposure value. Shorter exposure times are
kept as they are, as no exposure time avoids the bands there.

The default period of 10 ms matches 50 Hz mains. Flicker detection is
not implemented, so AeFlickerMode does not offer FlickerAuto.

Signed-off-by: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
